:name: m0900 AD9363 SPI capture (bring-up triggered)
:description: Boot m0900, then drive the radio bring-up that cold boot alone never reaches, and capture the AD9363 register sequence the firmware computes. See awto-au/awto-dji#2 + docs/phy-params.md.

# WHY a trigger is needed (static trace, scripts/re/m0900_trace.py):
# m0900 idles kicking the watchdog until a DUML cmdset-0x09 command arrives. The AD9363 is
# reached through the FPGA SPI bridge on SPI2 (renode/peripherals/AD9363SpiTap.cs). We call
# two functions directly instead of plumbing the DUML/UART path:
#   init_fpga_config  (0x0800d7c6)  FPGA tables + AD9363 base profile: a 2639-record script at
#                                   0x08016660 run by 0x0800d318 (decode: scripts/re/m0900_ad_script.py).
#                                   Includes the RF-PLL words (0x231.., 0x271..), BBPLL, filters, cals.
#   tcx_config_update1(0x0800f0bc)  TX attenuation update: writes AD9363 0x073/0x075 (boards 2/4/5)
#                                   from radio_state+0x11b. Writes no RF-PLL registers.
# Both need get_board_version (RAM 0x200000d8) in {2,4,5,6,7}; reads 0 in emulation, so we set it.
# tcx guards: active flag, "changed" check, FPGA reg 0xE9 bits 0 AND 1 (init_fpga_config writes 0x03).
# Which board code is the owned aircraft's P01007.06 is UNKNOWN (no source).

$fw ?= @firmware/P3X_FW_V01.11.0020_m0900.bin
$appBase ?= 0x08008000
$initcfg ?= 0x0800d7c6        # init_fpga_config: FPGA tables + AD9363 base profile
$tcxtune ?= 0x0800f0bc        # tcx_config_update1: TX attenuation update
$trap    ?= 0x2000FF00        # scratch RAM for a spin trap to catch each function's return
$board   ?= 0x02              # override with -e "$board=0x.." to try other AD9363 board codes

include @renode/peripherals/AD9363SpiTap.cs
mach create "m0900"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @renode/platforms/m0900.repl

sysbus LoadBinary $fw $appBase
sysbus.cpu VectorTableOffset $appBase

# Seed AD9363 status readbacks so every wait record in the init script completes.
# Poll records (op 0x0A @ 0x08016660 script, decoded by scripts/re/m0900_ad_script.py):
# wait until bit N of reg == v, 300 tries max. Values below satisfy all of them.
spi2.ad9363_spi2 SetReadDefault 0x05E 0x80    # BBPLL lock: bit7 == 1
spi2.ad9363_spi2 SetReadDefault 0x244 0x80    # RX CP cal valid: bit7 == 1
spi2.ad9363_spi2 SetReadDefault 0x284 0x80    # TX CP cal valid: bit7 == 1
spi2.ad9363_spi2 SetReadDefault 0x247 0x02    # RX VCO lock: bit1 == 1
spi2.ad9363_spi2 SetReadDefault 0x287 0x02    # TX VCO lock: bit1 == 1
spi2.ad9363_spi2 SetReadDefault 0x016 0x00    # CAL_CTRL busy bits self-clear: bits 7,6,4,1,0 == 0
spi2.ad9363_spi2 SetReadDefault 0x037 0x0A

# 1) Cold-boot init to its steady idle loop (deterministic sim time, not wall clock).
emulation RunFor "00:00:02"

# 2) Set the state the bring-up reads: board version, and tcx tune guards
#    ([0x20001ab4+0x119]=active=1, [+0x11b]=TX atten index=0xFF != applied [0x20000167]=0 so
#    the update is not skipped as "unchanged"; this forces 0xFF into AD9363 0x073/0x075).
sysbus WriteByte 0x200000D8 $board
sysbus WriteByte 0x20001BCD 0x01
sysbus WriteByte 0x20001BCF 0xFF
sysbus WriteByte 0x20000167 0x00
sysbus WriteWord $trap 0xE7FE

# 3) Phase A — init_fpga_config: FPGA config tables + AD9363 base profile script. LR -> spin trap.
sysbus.cpu SetRegisterUnsafe 14 0x2000FF01
sysbus.cpu PC $initcfg
emulation RunFor "00:00:03"

# 4) Phase B — tcx_config_update1: TX attenuation update (no RF-PLL writes).
sysbus.cpu SetRegisterUnsafe 14 0x2000FF01
sysbus.cpu PC $tcxtune
emulation RunFor "00:00:02"

# 5) Report which bus carried the AD9363 traffic and dump the capture. Output paths are
#    injected by the runner (scripts/re/m0900_capture.py) as absolute paths, because Renode
#    resolves relative write paths against its own binary dir, not the repo CWD.
echo "--- SPI1 (0x40013000) total / AD9363 ops ---"
spi1.ad9363_spi1 TransactionCount
spi1.ad9363_spi1 Ad9363Count
echo "--- SPI2 (0x40003800) total / AD9363 ops ---"
spi2.ad9363_spi2 TransactionCount
spi2.ad9363_spi2 Ad9363Count
spi1.ad9363_spi1 SaveCapture $cap1
spi1.ad9363_spi1 SaveRaw     $raw1
spi2.ad9363_spi2 SaveCapture $cap2
spi2.ad9363_spi2 SaveRaw     $raw2
quit
